# PLAN 3.4 matrix: OptTarget SPOT x mixed (TIP + h^4) DOF (CC 2026-10-11; the programmatic twins are
# tCalibMatrix / test_calib_matrix.py, TO).  The deck (tst_calib_mixed.in) is spoiled: TIP 1 mrad AND h^4 5e-3;
# CALIB must remove the spoil, print its merit and say why it stopped.  SPOT is the deck's own
# target; WFE / ZWF are selected through SETP (SETP offers WFE, ZWF and Beam -- not SPOT).
# DEADLINE: 120
# COPY: $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/tst_calib_mixed.in
# T = 35, not the deck's 10 (TO 2026-10-17): ONE residual (the spot radius) against two DOFs is a
# rank-1 Jacobian at every step and a round-off-sensitive path; it met T=10 only while the field
# weight was 0 (read as 1e-10, PLAN 1.2 (a)).  At weight 1, both compilers: T=10 TIP 1.46e-4,
# T=30 1.2e-9, T=35 6.0e-10 (h^4 9.7e-10), cap.  The bindings' twins set the same T.
! sed -i 's/^\(\s*OptMaxItrs=\).*$/\1 35/' $DECK
old $DECK
calib
no
yes
show 1
# EXPECT: Final LM merit \(chisq\) =\s+\S+
# EXPECT: Stopped: 
# EXPECT-NOT: Optimization aborted
# EXPECT-NOT: singular
# EXPECT: psiElt=\s+0\.0E\+00\s+(0\.0E\+00|-?\d\.\d+E-(09|[1-9]\d))\s+-\d\.\d+E\+00
# EXPECT: AsphCoef=\s+(0\.0E\+00|-?\d\.\d+E-(09|[1-9]\d))
# (measured 2026-10-11 at 338416c, both compilers: every cell stops at the cap T=10; TIP -> <= 1.8e-9, h^4 -> <= 3.3e-9, Z12 -> <= 5.5e-17)
